## Original work — MIT

Files: the models and symbols that no third-party heading below names, the
footprints that are not from the Keyswitch library, the scripts under `tools/`,
the documentation and the PCM metadata.

Evidence: the STEP `FILE_NAME` header names `Raul Mora` as author and `Kiboar`
as organization, and the symbols carry two hidden properties, `Author` and
`License`. `tools/provenance.py` writes both and `tools/lint.py` runs its
`--check`, so a missing stamp, or a stamp on a file listed as third-party,
fails the build.

Counts at the time of writing: 114 models and 131 symbols carry the stamp;
85 of the 199 models and 15 of the 146 symbols are third-party, and are listed
below. The stamp is not a blanket claim: it is the exact complement of this
file.

The STEP header is an ASCII field, so the author is spelled `Raul Mora` there.
`LICENSE` and this file keep the accented legal name.

