### Keyswitch KiCad Library — MIT OR CC BY-SA 4.0

Files: the switch, hotswap and stabilizer models under
`3dmodels/Kiboar_MechSwitch.3dshapes/`, `3dmodels/Kiboar_Cutout.3dshapes/` and
`3dmodels/Kiboar_Stabilizer.3dshapes/`, plus some of the footprints under
`footprints/Kiboar_MechSwitch.pretty/`, `footprints/Kiboar_Cutout.pretty/` and
`footprints/Kiboar_Stabilizer.pretty/`. The repository does not record which
footprints, so the whole library is credited rather than a guessed subset.

Evidence: all eleven of these models are byte-identical to files in the
upstream library, verified with SHA-256, and the STEP headers name
`kicad StepUp` with paths under `Switch_Keyboard_*`. The upstream repository
ships exactly eleven STEP models, so the match is complete rather than
sampled.

Source: <https://github.com/kiswitch/keyswitch-kicad-library>.
Licence: dual MIT / CC BY-SA 4.0 (`LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-CC-BY-SA`).

**Verdict: MIT-compatible** when attributed. Use the MIT option.

### KiCad official libraries — CC BY-SA 4.0 with exception

Files: twenty-four models come from the KiCad 10.0.8 library. Twenty-one are
byte-identical, verified with SHA-256 against the installed library:

- `3dmodels/Kiboar_Components.3dshapes/Battery_Holder_2032.step`,
  `LED_0805.step`, `LED_1206.step` and `Resistor_0805.step`
- `3dmodels/Kiboar_Led.3dshapes/LED_D3.0mm_{Blue,Clear,Green,Red,Yellow}.step`,
  `LED_D5.0mm_{Blue,Clear,Green,Red,Yellow}.step` and `LED_WS2812B.step`
- `3dmodels/Kiboar_Placeholder.3dshapes/Capacitor_0603.step`,
  `Capacitor_Disc_D3.0mm_W1.6mm_P2.50mm.step`,
  `Capacitor_Disc_D4.3mm_W1.9mm_P5.00mm.step`, `Diode_DO-35.step`,
  `Resistor_0805.step` and `Resistor_1206.step`

Three more — `3dmodels/Kiboar_Placeholder.3dshapes/Diode_SOD-123.step`,
`SOT-23-5.step` and `SOT-23-8.step` — carry the `kicad StepUp` copyright and
the CC BY-SA 4.0 notice in their own header. They are not byte-identical, so
they were re-exported or edited, but they are derived work and keep the same
licence.

`Kiboar_Components.3dshapes/Resistor_0805.step` is byte-for-byte the KiCad
`LED_0805_2012Metric.step`: the file has LED geometry under a resistor name.
The footprint does not reference it, and it is scheduled for replacement with
the other KiCad copies.

Footprints are different: none of the 1329 is byte-identical to the KiCad 10.0.8
library. The five that share a name with a KiCad footprint (`SOT-23-5`,
`SOT-23-6`, `SOT-23-8` and two mounting holes) have different content.

Source: <https://www.kicad.org/libraries/license/>. The KiCad exception lets the
files be used inside a design; it does not let the files themselves be
relicensed, so the twenty-four copied or derived models cannot be called MIT.

### Manufacturer CAD

Files: the models whose `FILE_NAME` field is a part number instead of a
design: `Kiboar_PinHeader.3dshapes/61000621121.step` and
`61001021121.step` (Molex), `Kiboar_Joystick.3dshapes/COM-10063.stp`
(SparkFun), `FJ08K-S.step` (Same Sky), `Kiboar_TRRS.3dshapes/PJ-320D.step`
(Same Sky) and `Kiboar_Placeholder.3dshapes/Fuse_PPTC1.stp`.

`Fuse_PPTC1.stp` is the one to look at first: its header declares
`LicenseCCBY-ND4.0` from `CADENAS`, and **CC BY-ND forbids derivative works**,
so it cannot sit in an MIT collection at all.

Many footprints and symbols also name a component vendor (Alps, Würth, Molex,
TE Connectivity, Kailh, E-Switch…) in their `Datasheet` or description. A
symbol drawn from a vendor datasheet is original work: the datasheet is the
reference, not the CAD.

Vendor terms commonly allow the model to be used in a design but do not grant
redistribution as a library. They were not verified vendor by vendor; treat
them as "used by permission for design work" until each vendor's terms are
checked.

